#if(v_ch11_saved_rose == 0) {
"Should we contact Daren and Hadrik?" Leila writes, hovering glowing blue script in the air as we reach the corridor arch. "They may have been trying our transceivers while we were away."

"Good idea," I say. "I'll raise them now."

I pull out my device and dial Daren first. I give him a quick, stripped-down summary—leaving out the machinery beneath the seredium tower—and assure him we made it back in one piece. He's been trying to reach us for over an hour. Once he agrees to meet us outside the infirmary, I dial Hadrik and repeat the brief account. He promises to meet us in ten minutes and cuts the connection.

The transceiver is barely back in my pocket when Daren steps out of the quarantine tunnel, holding Arraka's amulet right against his chin like a speaking trumpet while shouting into it. Kelrim trails a few paces behind, padding along in silence as they head our way.

}
#if(v_ch11_saved_rose == 1) {
