ID: B3-Ch05a-Mock
TEXT:

#if(v_ch11_saved_rose == 0) {
"What's wrong, Albert?" I call out. "Relegated to hallway guard? The underground's deadliest blade, playing nursemaid to refugees?"

Albert glares daggers at me, saying nothing, and brushes past without slowing down.

Hadrik chuckles. "You two really don't see eye to eye, do you?"

"Occupational hazard," I say. "Never had much luck with assassins."

The moment the heavy door seals behind us, we have Daren tend to Illuna. For all her iron composure, the puncture in her back from the teleporting guard is still bleeding through her tunic. Once the white glow finishes stitching muscle and skin, we wave Daren and Hadrik toward the bench.

When we finish laying out what we found beneath the seredium tower, the silence in the room splits three ways. Daren's jaw sets with grim, cold fury; Hadrik's face goes red with rage; and Arraka's amulet sits in utter, mocking indifference.

"Those absolute bastards!" Hadrik roars, slamming a fist into his palm. "Where is this cursed tower? I will tear the machine off its mountings with my bare hands!"

}
